{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall see My back, etc.</b> Now, with respect to El Elyon, one does not attribute to Him front and back; rather, His intent, may He be blessed, is toward the side of the life-force of the worlds, which stands in passionate desire to gaze upon His light, may He be blessed, and its sustainer is He, the Master, the Life of the Worlds. And this matter is among the things impossible — that any created being could possibly look upon His light, may He be blessed. Therefore HaShem prepared and made a screen through which one may gaze, and this is what He called אחוריים (My back), just as He did in His wisdom with man: the body is אחוריים (back) and the soul is its פנים (face), and the spirit is פנים to the soul, and the neshamah is פנים to the spirit. So too He prepared a light from Himself, may He be blessed, through which they may gaze and behold the Elohim, and this He called אחוריים. And the supernal light, which is stripped from the grasp of the soul of any living being, is called פנים (face). And this is what He said: <b>And you shall see My back, but My face shall not be seen.</b>" "And it is possible that He alluded to this by His placing the word <b>ופני</b> (and My face) immediately adjacent to <b>אחורי</b> (My back) — to say that even there too they are פנים (face); only that HaShem prepared them as אחוריים (back) so that they would be within the grasp of the prophets, as we have written." "Or perhaps He examined the fine point in saying <b>אחורי</b> (My back), to say that there are not many partitions and screens intervening as they are in the order of the prophets who gaze before HaShem, but only one specifically — and this is His saying <b>אחורי</b> (My back) and not אחורי אחורי (the back of My back). And whoever understands the matter of truth will bow and prostrate himself before the great El, and will diminish in his own eyes all his service, in proportion to the measure of grasp hoped for by a living soul according to its kind."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:36.710260054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}